---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="When Kind Finds Kind — Daf Yomi Game: Bekhorot 22"
  description="Bekhorot 22: watch a fetus vanish into the majority of a clot, wait for couriers from the Land of Israel to explain three skeins of yarn, test a sealed jar of fish brine in two possible worlds, pour it into a pot and watch nullified impurity wake up, and sort what may be done with a se'a of teruma lost in a hundred."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;500;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="frank min-h-screen bg-[#11131b] !text-[#ece6d8]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <header class="px-4 pt-12 pb-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm !text-[#9a98a8]">
          <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#363a4d] hover:!text-[#e0a84a]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>, Bekhorot 22, 10 October 2026
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl font-black leading-[1.05] sm:text-6xl">When Kind Finds Kind</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-2xl !text-[#e0a84a]" dir="rtl" lang="he">מָצָא מִין אֶת מִינוֹ וְנֵיעוֹר</p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed !text-[#cfcabd]">
          Today's daf is about things that disappear into a crowd. A fetus vanishes into a clot of blood. A dissolved child vanishes into
          an afterbirth. A little impure water vanishes into fish brine, and a se'a of teruma vanishes into a hundred se'a of ordinary
          grain. The majority swallows them, <em>bittul be-rov</em>. Then Rabbi Yirmeya asks what happens when the swallowed minority meets
          more of its own kind. In between, three skeins of yarn wait for someone to explain what they measure.
        </p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 600 110" class="mt-6 w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M10 98 H590" stroke="#363a4d" stroke-width="2" />
          <g fill="#c98b3a" opacity="0.9">
            <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="5" /><circle cx="78" cy="72" r="5" /><circle cx="96" cy="56" r="5" /><circle cx="70" cy="84" r="5" />
            <circle cx="104" cy="80" r="5" /><circle cx="88" cy="40" r="5" /><circle cx="120" cy="66" r="5" /><circle cx="54" cy="40" r="5" />
          </g>
          <circle cx="112" cy="46" r="5" fill="#6fa8c9" />
          <path d="M150 60 H230" stroke="#9a98a8" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 5" />
          <path d="M226 54 L236 60 L226 66" fill="none" stroke="#9a98a8" stroke-width="2" />
          <g fill="#6fa8c9">
            <circle cx="290" cy="58" r="5" /><circle cx="306" cy="74" r="5" /><circle cx="322" cy="50" r="5" /><circle cx="338" cy="80" r="5" />
            <circle cx="300" cy="88" r="5" /><circle cx="352" cy="62" r="5" /><circle cx="276" cy="76" r="5" /><circle cx="334" cy="36" r="5" />
            <circle cx="366" cy="84" r="5" /><circle cx="316" cy="64" r="5" /><circle cx="282" cy="40" r="5" />
          </g>
          <g fill="#c98b3a"><circle cx="350" cy="44" r="5" /><circle cx="370" cy="58" r="5" /></g>
          <circle cx="316" cy="64" r="9" fill="none" stroke="#c4553f" stroke-width="2.5" />
          <g transform="translate(470 58)" fill="none" stroke="#e0a84a" stroke-width="2.2">
            <ellipse rx="34" ry="26" /><ellipse rx="26" ry="19" /><ellipse rx="17" ry="12" /><ellipse rx="8" ry="6" />
            <path d="M-30 -12 C -6 -30 20 -20 32 -6" /><path d="M-32 6 C -10 22 18 24 33 8" />
          </g>
          <text x="88" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#9a98a8">swallowed</text>
          <text x="322" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#c4553f">…and woken</text>
          <text x="470" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#e0a84a">a skein</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm !text-[#9a98a8]" aria-live="polite">Score: <span id="tally"></span></p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-20">
      <!-- ============ Part I: clot ============ -->
      <section class="border-t border-[#262a3a] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p1">
        <h2 id="p1" class="text-3xl font-bold">I. Lost in the clot</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cfcabd]">
          Yesterday's mishna: a large animal expels a <em>ḥarrarat dam</em>, a clot of congealed blood. Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya'akov says it is
          buried, and the mother is exempt from the firstborn obligation, so her next calf is not a firstborn. Below is the clot as Rashi
          describes it: a little flesh inside a lot of blood and secretions. Rule on it.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 card">
          <canvas id="clotJar" width="560" height="200" class="w-full rounded" role="img" aria-label="A clot: a few pale flesh particles among many dark blood particles"></canvas>
          <p id="clotCap" class="mt-2 text-center text-sm !text-[#9a98a8]">pale = flesh of a fetus · dark red = blood and secretions</p>
        </div>
        <div id="clot" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part II: skeins ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#262a3a] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p2">
        <h2 id="p2" class="text-3xl font-bold">II. Three skeins, no labels</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cfcabd]">
          A woman whose fetus died inside her sits on the birthstool, the womb opens, and the house becomes impure as if the child were
          born there: <em>petiḥat ha-kever</em>, the opening of the grave. But a mishna (Oholot 7:4) says that for a stillborn this only applies
          once its head is rounded <em>ke-pika</em>, like a skein. Rav Huna: a skein of wool. Ḥiyya bar Rav: which one? A skein of the
          <em>warp</em> (שְׁתִי) is thin thread and small; a skein of the <em>woof</em> (עֵרֶב) is thicker and larger (Rashi). Rav Huna answers with
          a baraita. Light the lamp of every Sage who says the grave has opened.
        </p>
        <div id="sages" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>

        <h3 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">The couriers</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cfcabd]">
          Everyone remembers hearing about skeins. Nobody remembers what they were for. Send the couriers down the road from the Land of
          Israel to Babylonia one at a time, and label the skeins once someone can actually explain them (22a:7–8).
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 card">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 560 70" class="w-full" role="img" aria-label="The road from the Land of Israel to Babylonia">
            <path d="M30 40 C 150 10, 260 70, 380 34 S 510 30, 530 40" fill="none" stroke="#363a4d" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="3 7" />
            <text x="30" y="64" font-size="12" fill="#9a98a8" text-anchor="middle">ארץ ישראל</text>
            <text x="530" y="64" font-size="12" fill="#9a98a8" text-anchor="middle">בבל</text>
            <g id="rider" class="rider" style="transform: translate(530px, 40px)">
              <circle r="9" fill="#e0a84a" />
              <text id="riderTxt" y="-14" font-size="12" fill="#ece6d8" text-anchor="middle">Rav Huna</text>
            </g>
          </svg>
          <div id="courierLog" class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>
          <button id="nextCourier" class="act mt-3">Send the next courier →</button>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-4 card">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 560 170" class="w-full" role="img" aria-label="Three skeins of different sizes">
            <g id="sk0" transform="translate(95 80)"></g>
            <g id="sk1" transform="translate(255 80)"></g>
            <g id="sk2" transform="translate(445 80)"></g>
          </svg>
          <div id="slots" class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-2 text-sm"></div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm !text-[#9a98a8]">Labels (tap one, then tap a skein's slot):</p>
          <div id="tags" class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm"></div>
          <div id="tagOut" class="mt-3 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>
        </div>
        <div id="jug" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part III: brine ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#262a3a] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p3">
        <h2 id="p3" class="text-3xl font-bold">III. The sealed jar</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cfcabd]">
          Reish Lakish, in the name of Rabbi Yehuda Nesia: one who buys <em>tzir</em>, fish brine, from an <em>am ha-aretz</em> touches it to
          the water of a mikveh, and it is pure (22a:9). Brine always has some water in it. You can't see how much. So open both possible
          worlds. Blue dots are water, which can contract impurity (a red ring marks it impure). Amber dots are brine, which Rashi calls the
          fish's sweat: it can't contract impurity at all.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="card">
            <p class="text-sm font-bold !text-[#6fa8c9]">World A: mostly water</p>
            <canvas id="worldA" width="300" height="190" class="mt-2 w-full rounded" role="img" aria-label="World A jar"></canvas>
            <p id="capA" class="mt-1 text-sm !text-[#9a98a8]">impure water, a little brine</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <p class="text-sm font-bold !text-[#c98b3a]">World B: mostly brine</p>
            <canvas id="worldB" width="300" height="190" class="mt-2 w-full rounded" role="img" aria-label="World B jar"></canvas>
            <p id="capB" class="mt-1 text-sm !text-[#9a98a8]">a little impure water, mostly brine</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <button id="hashaka" class="act mt-3">Touch the jar to the mikveh (<span lang="he">הַשָּׁקָה</span>)</button>
        <div id="brine" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part IV: pot ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#262a3a] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p4">
        <h2 id="p4" class="text-3xl font-bold">IV. Bread or pot?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cfcabd]">
          Rabbi Yirmeya: they only taught this for dipping one's bread in the brine. Take World B, the one whose water was only
          <em>swallowed</em>, never purified, and use it two ways. Predict first, then watch.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 card">
          <canvas id="pot" width="560" height="210" class="w-full rounded" role="img" aria-label="The brine in use"></canvas>
          <p id="potCap" class="mt-1 text-center text-sm !text-[#9a98a8]">World B's brine, purified by the majority</p>
        </div>
        <div id="potQs" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part V: teruma ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#262a3a] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p5">
        <h2 id="p5" class="text-3xl font-bold">V. One in a hundred and one</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cfcabd]">
          Rav Dimi's proof (Terumot 5:2): a se'a of <em>impure</em> teruma fell into a hundred se'a of pure ordinary produce that had never been
          wetted. Find the teruma. You can't: once it's mixed, every grain looks the same.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 card">
          <canvas id="pile" width="560" height="170" class="w-full rounded" role="img" aria-label="One hundred and one se'a of grain"></canvas>
          <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <button id="mixBtn" class="act text-sm">Mix it in</button>
            <button id="liftBtn" class="act text-sm" disabled>Lift out one se'a</button>
          </div>
          <p id="pileCap" class="mt-2 text-sm !text-[#9a98a8]" aria-live="polite">One dark se'a of impure teruma, a hundred se'a of pure ḥullin.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="teruma" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
        <div id="kitchen" class="mt-5"></div>
        <div id="final" class="mt-6"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Learn ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#262a3a] pt-8" aria-labelledby="learn">
        <h2 id="learn" class="text-3xl font-bold">Learn the real daf</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#cfcabd]">
          Bekhorot 22 finishes Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya'akov's clot and turns it into a principle: Rabbi Yoḥanan reads both the clot and Rabbi
          Shimon's afterbirth as nullification by the majority. Then it detours through the skeins of Oholot 7:4 and the clod from a
          <em>beit ha-peras</em>, comes back by way of Reish Lakish's fish brine, and stops in the middle of Rav Dimi's proof. Rashi explains how
          <em>hashaka</em> purifies water and why it can't purify the brine; Rabbeinu Gershom walks through each step; the Niddah 27b parallel
          has Rabbi Shimon's afterbirth in full.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.22a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#e0a84a]/50 px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#e0a84a] hover:border-[#e0a84a]">Bekhorot 22 on Sefaria ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.22a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#262a3a] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9a98a8] hover:border-[#e0a84a]">Rashi ×36 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Bekhorot.22a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#262a3a] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9a98a8] hover:border-[#e0a84a]">Rabbeinu Gershom ×30 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Bekhorot.22a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#262a3a] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9a98a8] hover:border-[#e0a84a]">Steinsaltz ×14 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Bekhorot.22a.10.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#262a3a] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9a98a8] hover:border-[#e0a84a]">Tosafot ×11 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashash_on_Bekhorot.22a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#262a3a] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9a98a8] hover:border-[#e0a84a]">Rashash ×7 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah.27b.10" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#262a3a] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9a98a8] hover:border-[#e0a84a]">Niddah 27b: the afterbirth ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Oholot.7.4" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#262a3a] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9a98a8] hover:border-[#e0a84a]">Mishnah Oholot 7:4 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Terumot.5.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#262a3a] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9a98a8] hover:border-[#e0a84a]">Mishnah Terumot 5:2 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.23a.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#262a3a] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9a98a8] hover:border-[#e0a84a]">Continue: Bekhorot 23a ↗</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm !text-[#6f6d80]">
          Part of the <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#363a4d] hover:!text-[#9a98a8]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>,
          a new game from every daf. Texts and links via the Sefaria API.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style is:global>
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; }
    .opt, .act, .tag, .slot, .lamp {
      border-radius: 0.4rem;
      border: 1px solid #3a3f55;
      background: #11131b;
      color: #ece6d8;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      text-align: left;
      transition: border-color 0.15s, background-color 0.15s;
    }
    .opt:hover:not(:disabled), .act:hover:not(:disabled), .tag:hover:not(:disabled), .slot:hover:not(:disabled), .lamp:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: #e0a84a; }
    .opt:focus-visible, .act:focus-visible, .tag:focus-visible, .slot:focus-visible, .lamp:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #e0a84a; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .opt:disabled, .act:disabled, .tag:disabled, .lamp:disabled { opacity: 0.55; cursor: default; }
    .tag[aria-pressed='true'] { border-color: #e0a84a; background: #2a2316; }
    .slot { min-height: 3.6rem; text-align: center; border-style: dashed; }
    .slot:disabled { cursor: default; }
    .lamp { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; }
    .lamp .bulb { width: 0.9rem; height: 0.9rem; border-radius: 9999px; background: #2a2d3d; border: 1px solid #555a73; flex: none; }
    .lamp[aria-pressed='true'] .bulb { background: #e0a84a; border-color: #f4cf85; box-shadow: 0 0 10px #e0a84a; }
    .ok { border-color: #8fca9a !important; background: #15291b !important; opacity: 1 !important; }
    .bad { border-color: #c4553f !important; background: #2c1714 !important; opacity: 1 !important; }
    .card { border-radius: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #262a3a; background: #181b26; padding: 1rem; }
    .rider { transition: transform 1.4s ease-in-out; }
    .drop { animation: drop 0.45s ease-out; }
    @keyframes drop { from { transform: translateY(-12px); opacity: 0; } to { transform: none; opacity: 1; } }
    .crack { animation: crack 0.4s; }
    @keyframes crack { 25% { transform: translateX(-5px); } 75% { transform: translateX(5px); } }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .opt, .act, .tag, .slot, .lamp, .rider { transition: none !important; }
      .drop, .crack { animation: none !important; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!;
    const reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    const sef = (ref: string) => `https://www.sefaria.org/${ref.replace(/ (\d+[ab]?):/, '.$1.').replace(/ /g, '_')}`;
    const link = (ref: string) =>
      `<a href="${sef(ref)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#e0a84a] underline decoration-[#363a4d] hover:!text-[#f4cf85]">${ref} ↗</a>`;
    const good = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#b9e2c0]">✓ ${s}</p>`;
    const miss = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#f0bfb3]">✗ ${s}</p>`;
    const note = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#cfcabd]">${s}</p>`;
    const score: Record<string, [number, number]> = { clot: [0, 4], skein: [0, 8], brine: [0, 2], pot: [0, 3], teruma: [0, 8] };
    let finalShown = false;
    const tally = () => {
      const got = Object.values(score).reduce((a, [g]) => a + g, 0);
      const max = Object.values(score).reduce((a, [, m]) => a + m, 0);
      $('tally').innerHTML = `<span class="!text-[#e0a84a] font-bold">${got} / ${max}</span>`;
      if (finalShown) {
        const rank = got >= max - 3 ? 'Ravin, who finally explained the skeins' : got >= max / 2 ? 'Rav Dimi, who heard all three' : 'Rav Huna: "I heard, but I can\'t explain"';
        $('final').innerHTML = `<div class="card text-center"><p class="text-sm !text-[#9a98a8]">Final score</p>
          <p class="text-4xl font-black !text-[#e0a84a]">${got} / ${max}</p><p class="mt-1 !text-[#cfcabd]">Ranked: ${rank}.</p></div>`;
      }
    };
    tally();

    type Q = { q: string; opts: string[]; ans: number; why: string; ref: string };
    const ask = (host: HTMLElement, item: Q, bucket: string, after?: (right: boolean) => void) => {
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="!text-[#ece6d8]">${item.q}</p><div class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-1.5">${item.opts
        .map((o, j) => `<button class="opt text-sm" data-j="${j}">${o}</button>`)
        .join('')}</div><div class="out mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      host.appendChild(div);
      div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button.opt').forEach((b) =>
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const right = +b.dataset.j! === item.ans;
          div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button.opt').forEach((x) => {
            x.disabled = true;
            if (+x.dataset.j! === item.ans) x.classList.add('ok');
          });
          if (!right) { b.classList.add('bad'); div.classList.add('crack'); }
          else score[bucket][0]++;
          div.querySelector('.out')!.innerHTML = (right ? good(item.why) : miss(item.why)) + note(link(item.ref));
          tally();
          after?.(right);
        }),
      );
      return div;
    };
    const seq = (host: HTMLElement, items: Q[], bucket: string, done?: () => void) => {
      const step = (i: number) => {
        if (i >= items.length) return done?.();
        ask(host, items[i], bucket, () => step(i + 1));
      };
      step(0);
    };

    // ================= Particle jars =================
    type P = { x: number; y: number; vx: number; vy: number; c: string; ring: boolean; ringA: number; tc?: string };
    class Jar {
      ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D;
      w: number; h: number;
      ps: P[] = [];
      tint = '';
      wave = -1;
      constructor(public cv: HTMLCanvasElement) {
        this.ctx = cv.getContext('2d')!;
        this.w = cv.width; this.h = cv.height;
      }
      add(n: number, c: string, ring = false, area?: [number, number, number, number]) {
        const [x0, y0, x1, y1] = area ?? [14, 14, this.w - 14, this.h - 14];
        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++)
          this.ps.push({ x: x0 + Math.random() * (x1 - x0), y: y0 + Math.random() * (y1 - y0), vx: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.6, vy: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.6, c, ring, ringA: ring ? 1 : 0 });
        return this;
      }
      step() {
        for (const p of this.ps) {
          if (!reduced) {
            p.vx += (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.12; p.vy += (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.12;
            p.vx *= 0.96; p.vy *= 0.96;
            p.x += p.vx; p.y += p.vy;
            if (p.x < 8 || p.x > this.w - 8) p.vx *= -1, (p.x = Math.min(this.w - 8, Math.max(8, p.x)));
            if (p.y < 8 || p.y > this.h - 8) p.vy *= -1, (p.y = Math.min(this.h - 8, Math.max(8, p.y)));
          }
          const target = p.ring ? 1 : 0;
          p.ringA += reduced ? target - p.ringA : (target - p.ringA) * 0.06;
          if (p.tc) { p.c = p.tc; p.tc = undefined; }
        }
        if (this.wave >= 0) { this.wave += reduced ? this.h : 4; if (this.wave > this.h + 20) this.wave = -1; }
      }
      draw() {
        const g = this.ctx;
        g.fillStyle = this.tint || '#0d0f16';
        g.fillRect(0, 0, this.w, this.h);
        if (this.wave >= 0) {
          const grd = g.createLinearGradient(0, this.h - this.wave, 0, this.h - this.wave + 30);
          grd.addColorStop(0, 'rgba(111,168,201,0)'); grd.addColorStop(0.5, 'rgba(111,168,201,0.35)'); grd.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(111,168,201,0)');
          g.fillStyle = grd; g.fillRect(0, this.h - this.wave, this.w, 30);
        }
        for (const p of this.ps) {
          g.beginPath(); g.arc(p.x, p.y, 4.5, 0, Math.PI * 2); g.fillStyle = p.c; g.fill();
          if (p.ringA > 0.03) {
            g.beginPath(); g.arc(p.x, p.y, 8, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.strokeStyle = `rgba(196,85,63,${p.ringA.toFixed(2)})`; g.lineWidth = 2; g.stroke();
          }
        }
      }
    }
    const jars: Jar[] = [];
    const loop = () => { for (const j of jars) { j.step(); j.draw(); } if (!reduced) requestAnimationFrame(loop); };
    const redraw = () => { if (reduced) for (const j of jars) { j.step(); j.draw(); } };
    const WATER = '#6fa8c9', BRINE = '#c98b3a', FLESH = '#f0c9b8', BLOOD = '#7a1e24';

    // ================= Part I: clot =================
    const clotJar = new Jar($('clotJar') as HTMLCanvasElement).add(7, FLESH).add(64, BLOOD);
    jars.push(clotJar);
    const clotHost = $('clot');
    const verdictCard = () => {
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      const rows = [
        { k: 'b', q: 'Does it exempt the mother, so her next male is not a firstborn?', ans: true },
        { k: 't', q: 'Does it impart impurity by contact or carrying, as a carcass?', ans: false },
      ];
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="!text-[#ece6d8]">Between the mishna and the teaching of Rabbi Ḥiyya that goes with it (21b), the clot gets two rulings. Set each switch.</p>
        ${rows.map((r) => `<div class="mt-3"><p class="text-sm !text-[#cfcabd]">${r.q}</p><div class="mt-1 flex gap-2">
          <button class="opt text-sm" data-k="${r.k}" data-v="1">Yes</button><button class="opt text-sm" data-k="${r.k}" data-v="0">No</button></div></div>`).join('')}
        <div class="out mt-3 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      clotHost.appendChild(div);
      let done = 0, right = 0;
      rows.forEach((r) => {
        const btns = div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(`button[data-k="${r.k}"]`);
        btns.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const v = b.dataset.v === '1';
          btns.forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if ((x.dataset.v === '1') === r.ans) x.classList.add('ok'); });
          if (v !== r.ans) b.classList.add('bad'); else right++;
          if (++done === rows.length) {
            score.clot[0] += right === 2 ? 1 : 0;
            for (const p of clotJar.ps) if (p.c === FLESH) p.tc = '#a8454a';
            redraw();
            $('clotCap').textContent = 'the flesh is still there, but the majority has swallowed it';
            div.querySelector('.out')!.innerHTML = (right === 2 ? good : miss)(
              'Exempt, but not impure. The Gemara catches the tension: if it exempts from the firstborn, it must be a real offspring, so why no impurity? Rabbi Yoḥanan: <em>mi-shum bittul be-rov nag\'u bah</em>, the Sages applied nullification by the majority. Rashi: the flesh is nullified in the majority of blood and secretions that come out with it.',
            ) + note(link('Bekhorot 22a:2'));
            tally();
            next();
          }
        }));
      });
    };
    const CLOT_QS: Q[] = [
      {
        q: 'First, the hanging question from yesterday: why must the clot be <em>buried</em>, if it imparts no impurity?',
        opts: ['So that dogs and birds don\'t carry it to a house', 'To publicize that the mother is now exempt from the firstborn', 'Because it is a full corpse and needs burial', 'So the owner can\'t sell it as meat'],
        ans: 1,
        why: '<span lang="he">כְּדֵי לְפַרְסְמָהּ שֶׁנִּפְטְרָה מִן הַבְּכוֹרָה</span>: so people know the mother is exempt. Rashi: because we bury it, we treat it as an offspring, and nobody will think her next male is a firstborn.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 22a:1',
      },
    ];
    const PAIR_QS: Q[] = [
      {
        q: 'Rabbi Yoḥanan: "Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya\'akov and Rabbi Shimon said the same thing." Which ruling of Rabbi Shimon is the clot\'s twin?',
        opts: [
          'A kid less than eight days old enters the pen to be tithed',
          'An afterbirth in the house: the child dissolved before it came out',
          'A clod from a beit ha-peras imparts impurity at any size',
          'A se\'a of teruma lost in a hundred se\'a is always lifted out and burned',
        ],
        ans: 1,
        why: 'Niddah (27a): a woman miscarries an afterbirth and no child is visible in it. The first tanna: the house is impure, because there is no afterbirth without a child. Rabbi Shimon: <span lang="he">וָלָד נִימּוֹק עַד שֶׁלֹּא יָצָא</span>, the child dissolved before it came out. Rashi, from Niddah: his reason for a pure house is the same nullification by the majority. (The kid in the pen was yesterday\'s Rabbi Shimon, on a different subject.)',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 22a:4',
      },
      {
        q: 'So in that house with the afterbirth, who rules it pure?',
        opts: ['The first tanna, because the afterbirth itself is not a child', 'Rabbi Shimon, because the dissolved child is lost in the majority', 'Both, because no child was seen', 'Neither'],
        ans: 1,
        why: 'The first tanna says impure: "not because the afterbirth is a child, but because there is no afterbirth without a child." Rabbi Shimon agrees there was a child. He just says it dissolved and was swallowed.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 22a:4',
      },
    ];
    const next = () => seq(clotHost, PAIR_QS, 'clot');
    seq(clotHost, CLOT_QS, 'clot', verdictCard);

    // ================= Part II: sage lamps =================
    const SAGES = [
      { id: 'm', name: 'Rabbi Meir', he: 'פִּיקָּה שֶׁל שְׁתִי', rule: 'warp-skein head' },
      { id: 'y', name: 'Rabbi Yehuda', he: 'שֶׁל עֵרֶב', rule: 'woof-skein head' },
      { id: 'e', name: 'Rabbi Eliezer son of Rabbi Tzadok', he: 'מִשֶּׁיֵּרָאוּ טְפִיפִיּוֹת', rule: 'once tefifiyot are seen' },
    ];
    const CASES = [
      { t: 'The stillborn\'s head is rounded like a <strong>warp</strong> skein (the small one). The womb opens wide enough that its folds show.', on: ['m', 'e'] },
      { t: 'The head is rounded like a <strong>woof</strong> skein (the larger one). The womb opens wide enough that its folds show.', on: ['m', 'y', 'e'] },
      { t: 'The head is not yet rounded even like a warp skein, but the womb has opened so wide that <em>tefifiyot</em>, folds, are visible inside it.', on: ['e'] },
    ];
    const sagesHost = $('sages');
    const lampCase = (i: number) => {
      if (i >= CASES.length) {
        ask(sagesHost, {
          q: 'Shmuel, in the name of Rabbi Eliezer son of Rabbi Tzadok: "This is how they explained <em>tefifiyot</em> in Jerusalem." Like what?',
          opts: ['Rings in a cut tree trunk', 'A mule crouching to urinate: a skein seen within a skein', 'The folds of a Torah scroll\'s mantle', 'Threads bunched on a weaver\'s beam'],
          ans: 1,
          why: '<span lang="he">כִּפְרֵידָה שֶׁכּוֹרַעַת לְהַטִּיל מֵימֶיהָ, וְנִרְאֵית פִּיקָּה מִתּוֹךְ פִּיקָּה</span>. Rashi: a mule crouches lower than other animals, her womb opens wide, and folds appear in it, one ring inside another. <em>Tefifiyot</em> is <em>pika</em> twice over.',
          ref: 'Bekhorot 22a:6',
        }, 'skein');
        return;
      }
      const c = CASES[i];
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="text-sm !text-[#9a98a8]">Case ${i + 1} of ${CASES.length}</p><p class="!text-[#ece6d8]">${c.t}</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm !text-[#cfcabd]">Light every Sage who says the grave has opened:</p>
        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-1.5">${SAGES.map((s) => `<button class="lamp text-sm" aria-pressed="false" data-s="${s.id}"><span class="bulb"></span><span>${s.name} <span class="!text-[#9a98a8]">(<span lang="he" dir="rtl">${s.he}</span>)</span></span></button>`).join('')}</div>
        <button class="act mt-3 text-sm chk">Check the lamps</button><div class="out mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      sagesHost.appendChild(div);
      const lamps = div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.lamp');
      lamps.forEach((l) => l.addEventListener('click', () => l.setAttribute('aria-pressed', l.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true' ? 'false' : 'true')));
      const chk = div.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.chk')!;
      chk.addEventListener('click', () => {
        chk.disabled = true;
        let right = true;
        lamps.forEach((l) => {
          l.disabled = true;
          const should = c.on.includes(l.dataset.s!);
          const is = l.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true';
          if (should !== is) { right = false; l.classList.add('bad'); } else l.classList.add('ok');
          l.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(should));
        });
        if (right) score.skein[0]++;
        const names = SAGES.filter((s) => c.on.includes(s.id)).map((s) => s.name).join(', ');
        div.querySelector('.out')!.innerHTML = (right ? good : miss)(`Grave opened according to: ${names}. Rabbi Meir needs only the small warp skein, Rabbi Yehuda waits for the larger woof skein, and Rabbi Eliezer son of Rabbi Tzadok doesn't wait for the head at all: once the folds are seen, the grave is open (Rashi).`) + note(link('Bekhorot 22a:6'));
        tally();
        lampCase(i + 1);
      });
    };
    lampCase(0);

    // ================= Part II: couriers + skeins =================
    const SK = [
      { r: 26, name: 'שְׁתִי', en: 'warp skein' },
      { r: 38, name: 'עֵרֶב', en: 'woof skein' },
      { r: 58, name: 'סַקָּאִין', en: 'sack-makers\' great skein' },
    ];
    const drawSkein = (i: number, revealed: boolean) => {
      const g = $(`sk${i}`);
      const r = SK[i].r;
      let s = '';
      for (let k = 0; k < 5; k++) {
        const rr = r * (1 - k * 0.18);
        s += `<ellipse rx="${rr}" ry="${rr * 0.78}" fill="none" stroke="${revealed ? '#e0a84a' : '#555a73'}" stroke-width="2" />`;
      }
      s += `<path d="M${-r} ${-r * 0.3} C ${-r * 0.2} ${-r * 1.0}, ${r * 0.6} ${-r * 0.7}, ${r} ${-r * 0.1}" fill="none" stroke="${revealed ? '#f4cf85' : '#6f6d80'}" stroke-width="2" />`;
      s += `<text y="${r * 0.78 + 22}" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" fill="${revealed ? '#ece6d8' : '#6f6d80'}">${revealed ? SK[i].name : '?'}</text>`;
      g.innerHTML = s;
    };
    const skVisible = [false, false, false];
    SK.forEach((_, i) => drawSkein(i, false));
    const TAGS = [
      { id: 0, t: 'A woman\'s stillborn (opening of the grave)', sk: 0 },
      { id: 1, t: 'An animal\'s fetus', sk: 1 },
      { id: 2, t: 'A clod of earth from a beit ha-peras or the land of the nations', sk: 2 },
    ];
    let unlocked = 0; // number of tags available
    let picked: number | null = null;
    const placed = new Set<number>();
    const firstTry = new Set<number>();
    const tagsHost = $('tags'), slotsHost = $('slots');
    slotsHost.innerHTML = SK.map((s, i) => `<button class="slot" data-i="${i}" aria-label="Slot under the ${s.en}">—</button>`).join('');
    const renderTags = () => {
      tagsHost.innerHTML = TAGS.map((t) => {
        const locked = t.id >= unlocked;
        const done = placed.has(t.id);
        return `<button class="tag" data-t="${t.id}" aria-pressed="${picked === t.id}" ${locked || done ? 'disabled' : ''}>${locked ? '🔒 ' : done ? '✓ ' : ''}${t.t}</button>`;
      }).join('');
      tagsHost.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.tag').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        picked = +b.dataset.t!;
        renderTags();
      }));
    };
    renderTags();
    slotsHost.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.slot').forEach((s) => s.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (picked === null) { $('tagOut').innerHTML = note(unlocked ? 'Pick a label first.' : 'No one can explain these yet. Send a courier.'); return; }
      const t = TAGS[picked];
      const i = +s.dataset.i!;
      if (t.sk === i) {
        placed.add(t.id);
        if (!firstTry.has(t.id)) score.skein[0]++;
        s.innerHTML = `<span class="!text-[#b9e2c0]">${t.t}</span>`;
        s.classList.add('ok'); s.disabled = true;
        $('tagOut').innerHTML = good(t.id === 2
          ? 'The great skein of the sack-makers is the size of a clod of earth from a <em>beit ha-peras</em> (a field where a grave was plowed up) or from the land of the nations: big enough to impart impurity. It is like the seal of the <em>martzufin</em>, the big reed sacks Rashi says were sealed when closed.'
          : t.id === 0 ? 'A woman: like the warp skein. Ravin, explaining Rabbi Yoḥanan.' : 'An animal: like the woof skein. Ravin, explaining Rabbi Yoḥanan. Rashi: before that size, a fetus that died inside an animal is "swallowed" impurity, and a shepherd who reaches in and touches it stays pure.') + note(link(t.id === 2 ? 'Bekhorot 22a:8' : 'Bekhorot 22a:7'));
        picked = null;
        renderTags();
        tally();
        if (placed.size === 3) jugQ();
      } else {
        firstTry.add(t.id);
        s.classList.add('crack');
        setTimeout(() => s.classList.remove('crack'), 400);
        $('tagOut').innerHTML = miss('Not that skein. Remember Rashi: the warp skein is the small one, the woof skein the larger one.');
      }
    }));
    const COURIERS = [
      { who: 'Rav Huna', x: 530, say: '"I heard two skeins: one of warp and one of woof. <span lang="he">וְאֵין לִי לְפָרֵשׁ</span>, I can\'t explain them."', show: [0, 1], unlock: 0 },
      { who: 'Rav Dimi', x: 300, say: 'Rav Dimi arrives with Rabbi Yoḥanan\'s words: "I heard <em>three</em> skeins: warp, woof, and the great skein of the sack-makers. And I can\'t explain them."', show: [0, 1, 2], unlock: 0 },
      { who: 'Ravin', x: 530, say: 'Ravin arrives and explains in Rabbi Yoḥanan\'s name: <span lang="he">שֶׁל אִשָּׁה כְּשֶׁל שְׁתִי, שֶׁל בְּהֵמָה כְּשֶׁל עֵרֶב</span>. A woman\'s, like the warp; an animal\'s, like the woof.', show: [0, 1, 2], unlock: 2 },
      { who: 'The Gemara', x: 530, say: 'And the sack-makers\' skein? The Gemara knows it from a teaching on clods of earth (Tosefta Kelim).', show: [0, 1, 2], unlock: 3 },
    ];
    let ci = 0;
    const rider = $('rider');
    $('nextCourier').addEventListener('click', () => {
      const c = COURIERS[ci];
      $('riderTxt').textContent = c.who;
      if (c.who === 'Rav Dimi' || c.who === 'Ravin') {
        rider.style.transform = 'translate(30px, 40px)';
        setTimeout(() => (rider.style.transform = 'translate(530px, 40px)'), reduced ? 0 : 60);
      }
      c.show.forEach((i) => { skVisible[i] = true; drawSkein(i, true); });
      const p = document.createElement('p');
      p.className = 'drop !text-[#cfcabd]';
      p.innerHTML = `<strong class="!text-[#e0a84a]">${c.who}:</strong> ${c.say}`;
      $('courierLog').appendChild(p);
      unlocked = c.unlock;
      renderTags();
      ci++;
      if (ci >= COURIERS.length) { ($('nextCourier') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true; $('nextCourier').textContent = 'Everyone has arrived'; }
      else if (ci === 1 || ci === 2) $('nextCourier').textContent = 'Send the next courier from the Land of Israel →';
      else $('nextCourier').textContent = 'Ask about the third skein →';
    });
    const jugQ = () => ask($('jug'), {
      q: 'The baraita gives one more place to see that size. Where?',
      opts: ['The rim of a Bethlehem barley loaf', 'The top side of the stopper of a Bethlehem jug', 'The knot of a tefillin strap', 'The handle of a Jerusalem pitcher'],
      ans: 1,
      why: '<span lang="he">וְיֶשְׁנוֹ בְּצַד הָעֶלְיוֹן שֶׁל מְגוּפַת הֶחָבִית הַלַּחְמִית</span>. Rashi: the clay stopper was wide at the bottom and narrowed at the top so it could be gripped, and that top is the size. <em>Laḥmit</em>: made in Beit Leḥem.',
      ref: 'Bekhorot 22a:8',
    }, 'skein');

    // ================= Part III: two worlds =================
    const wA = new Jar($('worldA') as HTMLCanvasElement).add(46, WATER, true).add(14, BRINE);
    const wB = new Jar($('worldB') as HTMLCanvasElement).add(14, WATER, true).add(46, BRINE);
    jars.push(wA, wB);
    const brineHost = $('brine');
    $('hashaka').addEventListener('click', () => {
      ($('hashaka') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
      wA.wave = 0; wB.wave = 0;
      // World A: the brine is swallowed into the water, and the water is purified by touching the mikveh
      for (const p of wA.ps) { p.ring = false; if (p.c === BRINE) p.tc = '#8fb6c9'; }
      $('capA').textContent = 'mikveh touched: all water now, and pure';
      $('capB').textContent = 'mikveh touched… the water still bears its rings';
      redraw();
      seq(brineHost, [
        {
          q: 'World A, mostly water. Why is it pure now?',
          opts: ['The water was purified by touching the mikveh, and the brine is swallowed in the water', 'The water is swallowed in the brine', 'Brine purifies water', 'It isn\'t; it must be poured out'],
          ans: 0,
          why: '<span lang="he">אִי מַיָּא רוּבָּא נִינְהוּ, כֵּיוָן דְּעָבֵיד לְהוּ הַשָּׁקָה טָהֲרִי לְהוּ</span>. Rashi: the brine is nullified in the water, and water, unlike food, can be purified by <em>hashaka</em>: the jar is set in the mikveh until the mikveh water flows over its mouth and "kisses" the water inside.',
          ref: 'Bekhorot 22a:10',
        },
        {
          q: 'World B, mostly brine. Rashi says <em>hashaka</em> doesn\'t help here: the water is a minority inside a food. Is the brine impure?',
          opts: ['Yes: the impure water is still in it', 'No: the brine can\'t contract impurity, and the little water is swallowed by the majority of brine', 'Only if he cooks with it', 'It depends on how long it soaked'],
          ans: 1,
          why: '<span lang="he">צִיר לָא בַּר קַבּוֹלֵי טוּמְאָה הוּא… הָנָךְ בָּטְלוּ לְהוּ בְּרוּבָּא</span>. Whatever impurity there is sits only in the minority of water, and that water is nullified in the majority of brine. <em>Mi-mah nafshakh</em>: whichever world you are in, it\'s pure.',
          ref: 'Bekhorot 22a:10',
        },
      ], 'brine', () => {
        for (const p of wB.ps) if (p.c === WATER) { p.tc = '#b08a5a'; p.ring = false; }
        $('capB').textContent = 'the water vanishes into the brine: pure';
        redraw();
        potStart();
      });
    });

    // ================= Part IV: pot =================
    const pot = new Jar($('pot') as HTMLCanvasElement);
    jars.push(pot);
    const resetPot = () => {
      pot.ps = []; pot.tint = '';
      pot.add(14, '#b08a5a', false, [20, 20, 220, 190]).add(46, BRINE, false, [20, 20, 220, 190]);
    };
    resetPot();
    const potStart = () => {
      const host = $('potQs');
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      const uses = [
        { k: 'bread', label: '🍞 Dip bread in it', ans: false },
        { k: 'pot', label: '🍲 Pour it into a pot of water to cook', ans: true },
      ];
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="!text-[#ece6d8]">For each use, predict whether the brine ends up impure, then run it.</p>
        ${uses.map((u) => `<div class="mt-3"><p class="text-sm !text-[#cfcabd]">${u.label}</p><div class="mt-1 flex gap-2">
          <button class="opt text-sm" data-k="${u.k}" data-v="0">Stays pure</button><button class="opt text-sm" data-k="${u.k}" data-v="1">Becomes impure</button></div><div class="o-${u.k} mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div></div>`).join('')}`;
      host.appendChild(div);
      let n = 0;
      uses.forEach((u) => {
        const btns = div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(`button[data-k="${u.k}"]`);
        btns.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          btns.forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if ((x.dataset.v === '1') === u.ans) x.classList.add('ok'); });
          const right = (b.dataset.v === '1') === u.ans;
          if (!right) b.classList.add('bad'); else score.pot[0]++;
          resetPot();
          if (u.k === 'bread') {
            pot.add(1, '#d9b67a', false, [300, 80, 300, 80]);
            const loaf = pot.ps[pot.ps.length - 1];
            loaf.vx = 0; loaf.vy = 0;
            $('potCap').textContent = 'dipping bread: no water joins it, so the water stays swallowed';
            div.querySelector('.o-bread')!.innerHTML = (right ? good : miss)('<span lang="he">לֹא שָׁנוּ אֶלָּא לִטְבּוֹל בָּהֶן פִּיתּוֹ</span>: for dipping bread, Reish Lakish\'s ruling stands.') + note(link('Bekhorot 22a:11'));
          } else {
            pot.add(40, WATER, false, [260, 20, 540, 190]);
            const old = pot.ps.filter((p) => p.c === '#b08a5a');
            setTimeout(() => {
              for (const p of old) { p.tc = WATER; p.ring = true; }
              pot.tint = '#1a1117';
              $('potCap').textContent = 'the swallowed water found its kind: now the water outnumbers the brine, and the old impurity wakes';
              redraw();
            }, reduced ? 0 : 900);
            div.querySelector('.o-pot')!.innerHTML = (right ? good : miss)('<span lang="he">אֲבָל לִקְדֵירָה — לֹא, מָצָא מִין אֶת מִינוֹ וְנֵיעוֹר</span>. Rashi: the water in the brine meets the water in the pot, they join, outnumber the brine, and the impurity comes back and makes it impure.') + note(link('Bekhorot 22a:11'));
          }
          redraw();
          tally();
          if (++n === uses.length) proofQ();
        }));
      });
    };
    const proofQ = () => ask($('potQs'), {
      q: 'Rav Dimi was sitting and teaching this. Abaye: "Does nullified impurity really come back to life?" Rav Dimi: "And you don\'t hold that? Didn\'t we learn…" Which mishna does he cite?',
      opts: [
        'Red-heifer ashes mixed with ordinary ashes (Para 9:7)',
        'A se\'a of impure teruma that fell into a hundred se\'a of pure ḥullin (Terumot 5:2)',
        'Rabbi Shimon\'s afterbirth in the house (Niddah 18a)',
        'The clod from a beit ha-peras (Tosefta Kelim)',
      ],
      ans: 1,
      why: 'Terumot 5:2. Keep the red-heifer ashes in your pocket: that\'s Abaye\'s own comeback against Rabbi Yirmeya, on the next daf.',
      ref: 'Bekhorot 22a:11',
    }, 'pot', () => (($('mixBtn') as HTMLButtonElement).focus()));

    // ================= Part V: pile =================
    const pile = new Jar($('pile') as HTMLCanvasElement);
    jars.push(pile);
    const GRAIN = '#d9c9a0', TERUMA = '#7a1e24';
    for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) pile.ps.push({ x: 160 + (i % 20) * 19, y: 40 + Math.floor(i / 20) * 24, vx: 0, vy: 0, c: GRAIN, ring: false, ringA: 0 });
    pile.ps.push({ x: 70, y: 85, vx: 0, vy: 0, c: TERUMA, ring: true, ringA: 1 });
    const still = () => { for (const p of pile.ps) { p.vx = 0; p.vy = 0; } };
    still();
    const origStep = pile.step.bind(pile);
    let pileLive = false;
    pile.step = () => { if (pileLive) origStep(); else for (const p of pile.ps) { p.ringA += ((p.ring ? 1 : 0) - p.ringA) * (reduced ? 1 : 0.06); if (p.tc) { p.c = p.tc; p.tc = undefined; } } };
    $('mixBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
      ($('mixBtn') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
      pileLive = true;
      for (const p of pile.ps) { p.x = 20 + Math.random() * 520; p.y = 15 + Math.random() * 140; p.vx = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2; p.vy = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2; p.c = GRAIN; p.ring = false; }
      $('pileCap').textContent = 'Mixed. Which se\'a is the teruma? Nobody can say.';
      redraw();
      ($('liftBtn') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = false;
    });
    $('liftBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
      ($('liftBtn') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
      pileLive = false; still();
      const p = pile.ps[Math.floor(Math.random() * pile.ps.length)];
      p.x = 540; p.y = 20; p.tc = '#e0a84a';
      $('pileCap').textContent = 'One se\'a lifted out (top right). Is it the one that fell in?';
      redraw();
      seq($('teruma'), [
        {
          q: 'Rabbi Eliezer: what happens to the se\'a you lifted?',
          opts: ['It is ordinary produce now; eat it', 'It is treated as impure teruma and left to rot: "the se\'a that fell is the se\'a that rose"', 'It goes back into the pile', 'It is sold and the money given to a kohen'],
          ans: 1,
          why: '<span lang="he">תֵּירוֹם וְתֵרָקֵב, שֶׁאֲנִי אוֹמֵר: הִיא סְאָה שֶׁנָּפְלָה הִיא סְאָה שֶׁעָלְתָה</span>. Impure teruma may not be eaten, so it rots (Rashi).',
          ref: 'Bekhorot 22b:1',
        },
      ], 'teruma', kitchen);
    });

    const DISHES = [
      { t: 'Eat it dry (<span lang="he">נִיקּוּדִים</span>)', ok: true, why: 'Dry produce was never made susceptible, so the impure grain inside can\'t pass anything on (Rashi).' },
      { t: 'Eat it roasted (<span lang="he">קְלָיוֹת</span>)', ok: true, why: 'Roasting adds no liquid: still not susceptible.' },
      { t: 'Knead it with apple or mulberry juice', ok: true, why: 'Fruit juice doesn\'t make food susceptible to impurity (Rashi).' },
      { t: 'Knead it with water, in small doughs, never an egg-bulk in one place', ok: true, why: 'An egg-bulk is the least amount of food that can contract impurity.' },
      { t: 'Knead it with water into one big dough', ok: false, why: 'The Rabbis\' list keeps water away from the mixture unless it is split up.' },
      { t: 'Rinse the grain in water and leave it in a heap', ok: false, why: 'Water makes it susceptible, and that is exactly what the list avoids.' },
      { t: 'Knead it with wine', ok: false, why: 'Wine is one of the seven liquids that do make food susceptible (Makhshirin 6:4); only "fruit juices" are on the list.' },
    ];
    function kitchen() {
      const host = $('kitchen');
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="!text-[#ece6d8]">The Rabbis: <span lang="he">תַּעֲלֶה</span>, it is nullified, and the whole mixture is ḥullin. And yet it comes with a list of how to eat it. Mark each way of preparing the rest as allowed or not.</p>
        <div class="mt-3 space-y-3">${DISHES.map((d, i) => `<div><p class="text-sm !text-[#cfcabd]">${d.t}</p><div class="mt-1 flex gap-2">
          <button class="opt text-sm" data-i="${i}" data-v="1">Allowed</button><button class="opt text-sm" data-i="${i}" data-v="0">Not allowed</button></div><div class="o${i} mt-1 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div></div>`).join('')}</div>`;
      host.appendChild(div);
      let n = 0;
      DISHES.forEach((d, i) => {
        const btns = div.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(`button[data-i="${i}"]`);
        btns.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          btns.forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; if ((x.dataset.v === '1') === d.ok) x.classList.add('ok'); });
          const right = (b.dataset.v === '1') === d.ok;
          if (!right) b.classList.add('bad'); else score.teruma[0]++;
          div.querySelector(`.o${i}`)!.innerHTML = (right ? good : miss)(d.why);
          tally();
          if (++n === DISHES.length) cliff();
        }));
      });
    }
    const cliff = () => {
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop mt-5';
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="!text-[#ece6d8]">That is Rav Dimi's point. If the teruma were really gone, why keep water away from a mixture that is all ḥullin? Because the swallowed impurity might wake. ${link('Bekhorot 22b:2')}</p>
        <p class="mt-3 !text-[#cfcabd]">And then the daf stops in mid-sentence: <span lang="he" dir="rtl">וְתָנֵי עֲלַהּ: אוֹתָן חוּלִּין…</span> "And it is taught about it: those ḥullin…" ${link('Bekhorot 22b:3')}</p>
        <button class="act mt-3 text-sm" id="turn">Turn the page to 23a →</button><div id="turned" class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      $('kitchen').appendChild(div);
      $('turn').addEventListener('click', () => {
        ($('turn') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
        $('turned').innerHTML = note('…<em>according to Rabbi Eliezer</em>, what happens to them? The same list: dry, roasted, fruit juice, small doughs. Ulla gives the reason: a decree, in case someone brings a <em>kav</em> of impure ḥullin from somewhere else and a little more than a <em>kav</em> of this mixture, thinks the impure one is nullified by the majority, and the tiny bit of teruma in it finds its kind and wakes up. Abaye isn\'t convinced: "If impurity wakes impurity, does <em>purity</em> wake impurity?" The pot of fresh water was pure.') + note(link('Bekhorot 23a:1'));
        finalShown = true;
        tally();
      });
    };

    loop();
  </script>
</Layout>
